1
00:00:04,020 --> 00:00:04,890
No, seriously,

2
00:00:04,890 --> 00:00:07,170
I think I've finally figured out my problem with women.

3
00:00:07,170 --> 00:00:10,960
The capybara is the largest member of the rodent family.

4
00:00:11,410 --> 00:00:13,300
What does that have to do with me and women?

5
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:14,710
Nothing. It was a desperate attempt

6
00:00:14,710 --> 00:00:17,560
to introduce an alternate topic of conversation.

7
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:20,880
My problem is, I don't project confidence.

8
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:24,500
So I decided the next time I meet a woman I think is attractive,

9
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:26,740
rather than holding back and being cautious,

10
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:29,430
I'm going to assume the mantle of self-assurance.

11
00:00:29,430 --> 00:00:31,110
Oh, yeah? What's that look like?

12
00:00:35,020 --> 00:00:36,970
Hi.

13
00:00:36,970 --> 00:00:38,810
I'm Leonard.

14
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:41,370
And you are beautiful.

15
00:00:41,370 --> 00:00:45,030
You pop, sparkle and buzz electric.

16
00:00:45,030 --> 00:00:46,710
I'm going to pick you up at 8:00,

17
00:00:46,710 --> 00:00:50,500
show you a night you will never forget.

18
00:00:51,460 --> 00:00:53,560
Where are we going?

19
00:00:57,430 --> 00:00:58,600
Good news.

20
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:01,470
I made it onto the team for the new Defense Department

21
00:01:01,470 --> 00:01:03,410
laser-equipped surveillance satellite.

22
00:01:03,410 --> 00:01:04,740
Excuse me.

23
00:01:04,740 --> 00:01:07,000
If we're changing topics, I believe I have first dibs

24
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,010
with capybara, a rodent the size of a baby hippo.

25
00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:13,830
Congratulations, Howard.

26
00:01:13,830 --> 00:01:14,650
Thanks.

27
00:01:14,650 --> 00:01:17,000
Listen, I have to get a security clearance,

28
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,760
so you guys might be hearing from the FBI.

29
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:23,320
I don't want to speak to the FBI.

30
00:01:23,320 --> 00:01:24,030
Why not?

31
00:01:24,030 --> 00:01:26,780
I'm brown and I talk funny.

32
00:01:26,780 --> 00:01:28,990
They're just doing a background check on me.

33
00:01:28,990 --> 00:01:30,480
It doesn't matter, they'll find a reason

34
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:33,420
to give me a one-way ticket back to Gandhi-ville.

35
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:37,020
By the way, when I say that, it's not offensive.

36
00:01:37,020 --> 00:01:38,350
Don't be ridiculous, Raj.

37
00:01:38,350 --> 00:01:39,370
You're here legally.

38
00:01:39,370 --> 00:01:41,040
Nobody cares. Do you know how long it's been

39
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:42,410
since I got through airport security

40
00:01:42,410 --> 00:01:45,170
without being given a colonoscopy?

41
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:47,100
You know, I try very hard

42
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:49,880
to make our lunch hours educational and informative,

43
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:52,820
but your insistence on talking about your own lives

44
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:55,200
stymies me at every turn.

45
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:57,540
Fine, Sheldon, tell us about your giant rodents.

46
00:01:57,540 --> 00:01:59,700
No, you squandered your time with me,

47
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:01,700
and the moment has now passed.

48
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:03,330
Feast on your disappointment,

49
00:02:03,330 --> 00:02:06,460
much as the capybara feasts on its own waste.

50
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:40,000
Oh, Bella, don't you see?

51
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,130
Edward's only pushing you away because he loves you.

52
00:02:45,260 --> 00:02:46,570
Coming.

53
00:02:51,070 --> 00:02:53,170
Dr. Koothrappali?

54
00:02:54,490 --> 00:02:57,300
I'm Special Agent Page, FBI.

55
00:02:57,300 --> 00:02:58,850
May I come in?

56
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:03,960
I'd like to talk to you about Howard Wolowitz.

57
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:05,620
Oh, thank you.

58
00:03:06,170 --> 00:03:10,420
All right. Well, how long have you known Mr. Wolowitz?

59
00:03:31,430 --> 00:03:33,330
Rum cake?

60
00:03:33,330 --> 00:03:34,570
No, thanks.

61
00:03:34,570 --> 00:03:36,540
Now, about Mr. Wolowitz...

62
00:03:36,540 --> 00:03:37,970
Seven years.

63
00:03:37,970 --> 00:03:39,450
I see.

64
00:03:42,070 --> 00:03:44,810
I'm in this country legally, you know.

65
00:03:44,810 --> 00:03:46,400
I'm sure you are.

66
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:47,630
Now, to your knowledge,

67
00:03:47,630 --> 00:03:50,000
has Mr. Wolowitz ever committed a crime?

68
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:50,950
Of course not.

69
00:03:50,950 --> 00:03:52,530
I'm here on an H-1B visa,

70
00:03:52,530 --> 00:03:54,550
which means I can't be associated in any way

71
00:03:54,550 --> 00:03:57,650
with crime or criminal activity and I'm not.

72
00:03:57,940 --> 00:03:59,080
Good.

73
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:00,450
To your knowledge, does Mr. Wolowitz

74
00:04:00,450 --> 00:04:01,990
have any foreign contacts?

75
00:04:01,990 --> 00:04:03,940
No, just me.

76
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:06,070
Oh, there it is.

77
00:04:06,070 --> 00:04:08,720
Here comes a cavity search.

78
00:04:08,720 --> 00:04:09,430
Excuse me?

79
00:04:09,430 --> 00:04:11,580
Please don't send me back to India, it's so crowded!

80
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:14,240
It's like the whole country is one endless Comic-Con,

81
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:16,930
except everybody's wearing the same costume:

82
00:04:17,460 --> 00:04:19,610
Indian Guy.

83
00:04:19,610 --> 00:04:21,810
- Dr. Koothrappali, I'm not... - I love this country!

84
00:04:21,810 --> 00:04:23,660
The-the baseball, the freedom,

85
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:25,770
the rampant morbid obesity!

86
00:04:25,770 --> 00:04:28,290
From California to the New York Island!

87
00:04:28,290 --> 00:04:29,700
I'm a real Yankee Doodle boy!

88
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:30,740
Dr. Koothrappali, please.

89
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:34,410
My country 'tis of thee... ?

90
00:04:34,410 --> 00:04:36,420
...liberty

91
00:04:36,420 --> 00:04:39,460
It's really great.

92
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:43,550
So, when Howard said the FBI would be contacting me,

93
00:04:43,550 --> 00:04:46,220
I was expecting Mulder.

94
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:48,410
Glad to see I got Scully.

95
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:50,430
Who?

96
00:04:50,430 --> 00:04:52,200
Mulder and Scully.

97
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:54,390
X-Files.

98
00:04:54,390 --> 00:04:56,280
"The truth is out there." never mind.

99
00:04:56,280 --> 00:05:00,330
Uh, so, what would you like to know?

100
00:05:00,330 --> 00:05:03,220
You work with Mr. Wolowitz here at the university, correct?

101
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:05,490
Yes. Of course, we're in different departments.

102
00:05:05,490 --> 00:05:08,530
He's an engineer and I'm an experimental physicist.

103
00:05:08,530 --> 00:05:09,660
You know, one of those guys

104
00:05:09,660 --> 00:05:11,860
who examines the building blocks of creation

105
00:05:11,860 --> 00:05:14,930
and says, "Hello, maker of the universe.

106
00:05:16,410 --> 00:05:18,420
"I see what you did there.

107
00:05:18,420 --> 00:05:20,420
Good one."

108
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:21,680
Right.

109
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:23,000
Now, how would you characterize

110
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,800
your relationship with Mr. Wolowitz?

111
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:27,700
Good.

112
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:29,960
It's a good relationship.

113
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:32,890
Of course, most of my relationships are good.

114
00:05:32,890 --> 00:05:36,470
Probably because I exude confidence.

115
00:05:36,470 --> 00:05:39,010
People are drawn to that, you know?

116
00:05:40,430 --> 00:05:42,750
Confidence, not exuding.

117
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:47,190
Do you know of any groups Mr. Wolowitz is a member of?

118
00:05:47,190 --> 00:05:50,330
You are beautiful, you know that?

119
00:05:50,330 --> 00:05:54,930
You pop, sparkle and buzz electric.

120
00:05:56,500 --> 00:05:58,850
I'm going to pick you up at 8:00,

121
00:05:58,850 --> 00:06:02,890
show you a night you will never forget.

122
00:06:02,890 --> 00:06:04,780
Sounds great.

123
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:06,500
Really?

124
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,390
Can my six-foot-two

125
00:06:09,390 --> 00:06:12,170
Navy seal husband come with us?

126
00:06:13,310 --> 00:06:13,760
Is that...?

127
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:17,370
Oh, my, I didn't see the ring with my glasses off, so...

128
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:20,420
Look at that, I'm starting to exude.

129
00:06:23,940 --> 00:06:25,320
Want to get that?

130
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:27,060
Not particularly.

131
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:29,930
Could you get that?

132
00:06:29,930 --> 00:06:32,690
I suppose I could if I were asked.

133
00:06:33,410 --> 00:06:35,160
Would you please get that?

134
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:37,380
Of course.

135
00:06:38,450 --> 00:06:41,320
Why do you have to make things so complicated?

136
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:43,980
Dr. Cooper?

137
00:06:43,980 --> 00:06:44,760
Yes.

138
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:47,540
I'm Special Agent Page, FBI.

139
00:06:50,650 --> 00:06:52,050
You say you're

140
00:06:52,050 --> 00:06:54,740
Special Agent Page, FBI.

141
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:56,590
Here's my I.D.

142
00:06:56,590 --> 00:07:00,990
And here is my Justice League membership card.

143
00:07:03,210 --> 00:07:06,240
But that doesn't prove I know Batman.

144
00:07:06,870 --> 00:07:08,870
I just want to ask you a few questions

145
00:07:08,870 --> 00:07:10,820
about Howard Wolowitz.

146
00:07:10,820 --> 00:07:13,380
Oh. All right.

147
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,090
I doubt anyone would risk

148
00:07:15,090 --> 00:07:18,000
the stiff penalties for impersonating a federal officer

149
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,180
just to ask questions about a minor league engineer

150
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:22,840
with an unresolved oedipal complex.

151
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:25,030
Thank you.

152
00:07:25,030 --> 00:07:28,240
For the record, I truly support the FBI

153
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:30,030
in the mission which is expressed

154
00:07:30,030 --> 00:07:31,630
through their motto...?

155
00:07:31,630 --> 00:07:33,960
Fidelity, bravery, and integrity.

156
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:35,840
Correct. Now to business.

157
00:07:36,710 --> 00:07:40,990
18 years ago, I sent the FBI crime lab samples

158
00:07:40,990 --> 00:07:43,430
from a bag of excrement that had been lit on fire

159
00:07:43,430 --> 00:07:46,780
on my front porch...

160
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:50,480
...for fingerprinting and DNA analysis.

161
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:52,880
Why haven't I heard back yet?

162
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:56,960
Well, the FBI crime lab does have a lot on its plate.

163
00:07:56,960 --> 00:07:58,710
That's of little comfort to a nation

164
00:07:58,710 --> 00:08:02,510
attempting to scrape burning feces off its shoes.

165
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:05,960
Would you mind if we talked about Mr. Wolowitz now?

166
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:08,320
A little, but go on.

167
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:09,470
Thank you.

168
00:08:09,470 --> 00:08:12,810
Would you characterize him as responsible?

169
00:08:13,550 --> 00:08:17,320
I'm going to answer that with a visual aid.

170
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:19,880
This is my nine-disc complete

171
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:22,250
Lord of the Rings trilogy blu-ray set.

172
00:08:22,250 --> 00:08:24,580
Mr. Wolowitz borrowed it,

173
00:08:24,580 --> 00:08:28,390
damaged plastic retention hub number three...

174
00:08:32,540 --> 00:08:35,440
...and then returned it to me, hoping I wouldn't notice.

175
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:39,230
Would you characterize that as responsible?

176
00:08:39,230 --> 00:08:42,860
That's really not the sort of thing we're interested in.

177
00:08:42,860 --> 00:08:45,730
You heard me say blu-ray, right?

178
00:08:45,730 --> 00:08:47,610
I did.

179
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:48,610
Very well.

180
00:08:48,610 --> 00:08:50,050
Would you be interested

181
00:08:50,050 --> 00:08:52,520
in knowing that Mr. Wolowitz once snuck onto

182
00:08:52,520 --> 00:08:55,480
my World of Warcraft account and changed the name

183
00:08:55,480 --> 00:09:00,360
of a certain level-80 warlock from Sheldor to Smeldor?

184
00:09:01,010 --> 00:09:02,330
I'm afraid not.

185
00:09:02,330 --> 00:09:04,010
Is there anything else?

186
00:09:04,010 --> 00:09:05,040
"Is there anything else"?

187
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:06,320
Where would you like to start?

188
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:08,060
He refuses to pay fines

189
00:09:08,060 --> 00:09:10,060
when he's overdue with books I lend him.

190
00:09:10,060 --> 00:09:11,490
He crashed the Mars Rover

191
00:09:11,490 --> 00:09:13,230
while attempting to impress a woman.

192
00:09:13,230 --> 00:09:14,660
He recommended that I go see

193
00:09:14,660 --> 00:09:17,370
the third Matrix movie because it was, and I quote,

194
00:09:17,370 --> 00:09:20,250
"just as good as the first one".

195
00:09:20,850 --> 00:09:24,430
If that's not irresponsible, I don't know what is.

196
00:09:24,430 --> 00:09:26,750
The Mars Rover?

197
00:09:32,180 --> 00:09:33,830
Did I say Mars Rover?

198
00:09:33,830 --> 00:09:35,290
You did.

199
00:09:35,290 --> 00:09:36,940
That was actually a poorly chosen example,

200
00:09:36,940 --> 00:09:39,620
as it had nothing to do with me.

201
00:09:40,090 --> 00:09:42,220
Yes, well, let's talk about it anyway.

202
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:44,130
I don't want to.

203
00:09:44,650 --> 00:09:46,080
Not that my disinclination

204
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:48,460
to discuss the topic should be interpreted as evidence of

205
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:50,590
Howard Wolowitz's culpability in the destruction

206
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:53,710
of government property worth millions of dollars.

207
00:09:53,710 --> 00:09:55,140
Thank you, Dr. Cooper.

208
00:09:55,140 --> 00:09:56,740
I think I have all I need.

209
00:09:56,740 --> 00:09:58,610
Oh, good.

210
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:00,210
I was afraid you were going to fixate

211
00:10:00,210 --> 00:10:02,400
on that Mars Rover incident.

212
00:10:08,550 --> 00:10:09,790
Hey, buddies.

213
00:10:09,790 --> 00:10:11,370
Guess who didn't get security clearance

214
00:10:11,370 --> 00:10:13,310
to work on the giant space laser?

215
00:10:13,310 --> 00:10:14,130
What happened?

216
00:10:14,130 --> 00:10:16,420
Apparently, the background interviews didn't go well.

217
00:10:16,420 --> 00:10:20,010
You guys wouldn't know anything about that, would you?

218
00:10:21,220 --> 00:10:23,070
Well, actually, I may have gotten

219
00:10:23,070 --> 00:10:25,510
a little tipsy when I talked to her.

220
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:28,890
And I may have hit on her a little bit.

221
00:10:29,410 --> 00:10:32,390
I may have thrown up rum cake on her shoes.

222
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:34,020
I see.

223
00:10:34,020 --> 00:10:36,350
Well, it's good to know, when I need you guys,

224
00:10:36,350 --> 00:10:40,150
I can always count on you to step up and ruin everything.

225
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:43,710
I feel awful.

226
00:10:43,710 --> 00:10:45,150
Ah, me, too.

227
00:10:45,150 --> 00:10:45,750
To tell you the truth,

228
00:10:45,750 --> 00:10:46,650
I thought if anyone was going to

229
00:10:46,650 --> 00:10:49,730
screw things up for Howard, it'd be Sheldon.

230
00:10:50,450 --> 00:10:53,830
Well, your expectations have been subverted.

231
00:10:54,190 --> 00:10:55,870
Aha.

232
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:05,020
What are you doing up?

233
00:11:05,020 --> 00:11:07,000
Sleep eludes me, Leonard.

234
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,450
Really?

235
00:11:08,450 --> 00:11:11,070
Maybe sleep has met you before.

236
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:12,580
Mockery?

237
00:11:12,580 --> 00:11:14,210
That's all you have to offer?

238
00:11:14,210 --> 00:11:15,760
I'm sorry. Why can't you sleep?

239
00:11:15,760 --> 00:11:16,930
Who knows?

240
00:11:16,930 --> 00:11:19,680
I haven't watched any scary movies recently.

241
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:22,200
I'm no longer obsessing over why the predicted mass

242
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:24,250
of the quantum vacuum has little effect

243
00:11:24,250 --> 00:11:26,170
on the expansion of the universe.

244
00:11:26,170 --> 00:11:29,620
And it's been weeks since I took that accidental sip of Red Bull.

245
00:11:30,660 --> 00:11:32,550
Did something happen today that's bothering you?

246
00:11:32,550 --> 00:11:34,500
Well, I did mention

247
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:37,420
the Mars Rover incident to that FBI agent

248
00:11:37,420 --> 00:11:40,050
and probably cost Howard his security clearance.

249
00:11:40,050 --> 00:11:42,630
- What? - But why should that keep me up?

250
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:45,930
Because you feel guilty?

251
00:11:45,930 --> 00:11:47,590
Interesting.

252
00:11:47,590 --> 00:11:51,880
So you're saying my insomnia is caused by a guilty conscience.

253
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:53,730
Actually, you don't have insomnia.

254
00:11:53,730 --> 00:11:54,960
You're sleeping now.

255
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:56,160
Excuse me?

256
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:58,090
You're having a guilt-ridden dream.

257
00:11:58,090 --> 00:12:00,880
Do you have any evidence to support that hypothesis?

258
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:03,570
How about that Gorn sitting on the couch?

259
00:12:07,240 --> 00:12:09,350
That seems fairly conclusive.

260
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:12,600
No, Gorn, no.

261
00:12:13,560 --> 00:12:15,920
That's where I sit.

262
00:12:17,920 --> 00:12:20,980
Thank you for agreeing to see me, Agent Page.

263
00:12:20,980 --> 00:12:24,810
Thank you for filing a complaint with my superior, Dr. Cooper.

264
00:12:25,850 --> 00:12:27,200
I understand you want to recant

265
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:29,250
your statement about Howard Wolowitz.

266
00:12:29,250 --> 00:12:32,540
- Yes. - Was your statement untrue?

267
00:12:32,540 --> 00:12:33,970
No.

268
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:36,890
Then I'm afraid you can't withdraw it.

269
00:12:36,890 --> 00:12:41,040
I'm sorry. I don't recall you saying "No backsies."

270
00:12:42,310 --> 00:12:43,650
Is there anything else?

271
00:12:43,650 --> 00:12:46,630
Yes. I'd like to offer a laudatory statement

272
00:12:46,630 --> 00:12:48,940
about Howard's many excellent qualities that I believe

273
00:12:48,940 --> 00:12:51,480
will tip the scales back in his favor.

274
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:53,410
"Howard Joel Wolowitz.

275
00:12:53,410 --> 00:12:56,820
"H is for honesty, of which he has much.

276
00:12:56,820 --> 00:12:58,440
"O's for outstanding,

277
00:12:58,440 --> 00:12:59,700
"Which he is such.

278
00:12:59,700 --> 00:13:02,360
"W's for witty, he's quick with a joke.

279
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:04,490
- A's for artistic, his ability..." - I'm sorry.

280
00:13:04,490 --> 00:13:07,500
Dr. Cooper, this matter is already closed.

281
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:10,930
But I still have "rd Joel Wolowitz" Left to go.

282
00:13:10,930 --> 00:13:12,790
It's closed.

283
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:15,470
I don't understand why you people

284
00:13:15,470 --> 00:13:16,980
are picking on my friend, Howard,

285
00:13:16,980 --> 00:13:19,560
when there are much more serious security threats to pursue.

286
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:21,660
For instance, when I first met Leonard,

287
00:13:21,660 --> 00:13:23,020
he was on the verge of giving away

288
00:13:23,020 --> 00:13:25,170
rocket secrets to a North Korean spy,

289
00:13:25,170 --> 00:13:28,340
and not one agent ever investigated that.

290
00:13:29,090 --> 00:13:31,350
This is Leonard Hofstadter?

291
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:33,410
No, it's a different Leonard.

292
00:13:33,410 --> 00:13:34,740
He's...

293
00:13:34,740 --> 00:13:37,360
Chinese, red hair, six fingers. Good-bye.

294
00:13:40,960 --> 00:13:42,330
Raj.

295
00:13:42,330 --> 00:13:43,790
Have you seen Howard?

296
00:13:43,790 --> 00:13:45,630
I think he's eating lunch.

297
00:13:45,630 --> 00:13:48,290
Uh, Sheldon, I want you to meet Neil DeGrasse Tyson

298
00:13:48,290 --> 00:13:50,440
from the Hayden Planetarium in New York.

299
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:52,720
I'm quite familiar with Dr. Tyson.

300
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:55,010
He's responsible for the demotion of Pluto

301
00:13:55,010 --> 00:13:56,690
from planetary status.

302
00:13:56,690 --> 00:13:59,280
I liked Pluto.

303
00:13:59,280 --> 00:14:01,630
Ergo I do not like you.

304
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:03,680
But I actually didn't demote Pluto.

305
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:06,350
That was a vote of the International Astronomical Union.

306
00:14:06,350 --> 00:14:08,510
If "Ifs" And "Buts" Were candy and nuts,

307
00:14:08,510 --> 00:14:11,000
we'd all have a merry Christmas.

308
00:14:11,940 --> 00:14:14,290
Think about that, Dr. Tyson.

309
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:17,310
Is that the guy you were telling me about?

310
00:14:17,310 --> 00:14:19,310
Oh, yeah.

311
00:14:21,180 --> 00:14:22,640
Howard.

312
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:27,150
The person at fault for you not getting a security clearance is me.

313
00:14:27,150 --> 00:14:28,020
You?

314
00:14:28,020 --> 00:14:30,150
Yes, but before you get upset, I want you to know

315
00:14:30,150 --> 00:14:33,630
I went to the FBI and retracted my statement.

316
00:14:33,630 --> 00:14:35,750
And they were okay with that?

317
00:14:35,750 --> 00:14:38,370
No. If anything, I made it worse.

318
00:14:38,870 --> 00:14:41,760
In any case, I have been riddled with guilt,

319
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:44,390
which is causing Gorn-infested REM sleep.

320
00:14:44,390 --> 00:14:48,980
So, I'm here now to say I'm sorry.

321
00:14:48,980 --> 00:14:49,930
Are you kidding me?

322
00:14:49,930 --> 00:14:52,480
You've set my career back at least two years,

323
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:55,570
and you think you can make it right with "I'm sorry"?

324
00:14:55,570 --> 00:14:57,230
Yes.

325
00:14:57,230 --> 00:14:58,920
I followed the social protocol.

326
00:14:58,920 --> 00:15:01,700
I attempted to right the wrong, and when I failed to do so,

327
00:15:01,700 --> 00:15:03,420
I delivered a heartfelt apology.

328
00:15:03,420 --> 00:15:04,470
Now you say,

329
00:15:04,470 --> 00:15:05,600
"Apology accepted,"

330
00:15:05,600 --> 00:15:09,350
and I will offer you a one-time-only high five.

331
00:15:10,720 --> 00:15:13,310
Your apology is not accepted.

332
00:15:13,310 --> 00:15:14,060
You're tricking me.

333
00:15:14,060 --> 00:15:15,680
It really is, isn't it?

334
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:18,030
Leave me alone, Sheldon.

335
00:15:20,430 --> 00:15:22,230
Dr. Cooper, I just wanted you to know

336
00:15:22,230 --> 00:15:25,630
I'm sorry for the role I played in the Pluto matter.

337
00:15:25,630 --> 00:15:27,600
Oh, shut up.

338
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:33,290
Sheldon?

339
00:15:33,290 --> 00:15:35,050
Hello.

340
00:15:35,050 --> 00:15:36,860
What are you doing here?

341
00:15:36,860 --> 00:15:39,300
I have troubles, Penny.

342
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:40,390
I've come to pour them out

343
00:15:40,390 --> 00:15:43,300
to the sympathetic ear of the local barkeep.

344
00:15:43,300 --> 00:15:46,670
You know, they have a really nice bar over at the Olive Garden.

345
00:15:47,270 --> 00:15:49,030
I don't like the Olive Garden.

346
00:15:49,030 --> 00:15:51,470
They treat me like family.

347
00:15:53,690 --> 00:15:56,910
- Okay, Sheldon. What can I get you?  - Alcohol.

348
00:15:57,290 --> 00:15:58,730
Could you be a little more specific?

349
00:15:58,730 --> 00:16:01,170
Ethyl alcohol.

350
00:16:01,170 --> 00:16:03,070
40 milliliters.

351
00:16:03,070 --> 00:16:05,000
I'm sorry, honey. I don't know milliliters.

352
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:08,510
Ah. Blame President James "Jimmy" Carter.

353
00:16:08,510 --> 00:16:11,110
He started America on a path to the metric system

354
00:16:11,110 --> 00:16:12,960
but then just gave up.

355
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:15,550
He wonders why he was a one-term president.

356
00:16:16,410 --> 00:16:18,420
Would you say that's about 40 milliliters?

357
00:16:18,420 --> 00:16:20,480
- More or less.  - Great.

358
00:16:22,570 --> 00:16:23,780
Now, where were we?

359
00:16:23,780 --> 00:16:26,650
I believe you were about to ask me to choose a cocktail.

360
00:16:26,650 --> 00:16:30,000
Fortunately, thanks to computer-savvy alcoholics,

361
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,140
there's an app for that.

362
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:34,150
Let's see.

363
00:16:34,150 --> 00:16:36,290
Harvey Wallbanger. Eh.

364
00:16:36,290 --> 00:16:39,590
Sex on the Beach. I hardly think so.

365
00:16:39,590 --> 00:16:43,210
Rob Roy, silk Slipper, Mad Hatter.

366
00:16:43,210 --> 00:16:46,850
I'll have a Rosewater Ricky.

367
00:16:46,850 --> 00:16:50,540
- A what? - You'll need pitted,brandied cherries, gin,

368
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:54,170
rosewater, Angostura Bitters and overproofed rum.

369
00:16:54,170 --> 00:16:56,650
Now, first, dust the cherries with sugar,

370
00:16:56,650 --> 00:16:59,430
then spray them with a mixture of rum and bitters.

371
00:16:59,430 --> 00:17:00,810
Then ignite the rum, caramel...

372
00:17:00,810 --> 00:17:03,830
Here you go -- one Rosewater Ricky.

373
00:17:03,830 --> 00:17:05,920
That's not how it looks in the picture.

374
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:08,290
Oh, yeah, you know, every bartender makes it differently.

375
00:17:08,290 --> 00:17:10,080
Why don't you give it a try.

376
00:17:10,470 --> 00:17:12,130
All right.

377
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:15,880
To the metric system.

378
00:17:26,380 --> 00:17:28,490
I can't taste the cherries.

379
00:17:30,750 --> 00:17:33,670
All right. Sheldon, what's on your mind?

380
00:17:33,670 --> 00:17:36,890
I wronged Howard, and he won't accept my apology.

381
00:17:36,890 --> 00:17:38,050
Oh, right, that.

382
00:17:38,050 --> 00:17:40,670
Yes, Leonard told me. Sorry, honey.

383
00:17:40,670 --> 00:17:45,380
Penny, you face failure on a daily basis.

384
00:17:45,380 --> 00:17:46,760
How do you cope?

385
00:17:46,760 --> 00:17:48,240
I drink.

386
00:17:50,170 --> 00:17:51,960
To drinking.

387
00:17:55,130 --> 00:17:57,310
Nope.

388
00:18:00,130 --> 00:18:03,510
If only there were some way to force Howard to accept my apology

389
00:18:03,510 --> 00:18:06,450
so I could escape this miasma of guilt.

390
00:18:06,450 --> 00:18:08,340
You know, sometimes stuff just happens,

391
00:18:08,340 --> 00:18:09,870
and there's nothing you can do about it.

392
00:18:09,870 --> 00:18:12,840
Lisa Peterson hasn't talked to me since the 11th grade,

393
00:18:12,840 --> 00:18:14,620
because no matter how much you apologize,

394
00:18:14,620 --> 00:18:17,720
you can't go back and un-dry-hump someone's boyfriend.

395
00:18:19,350 --> 00:18:20,640
I see.

396
00:18:20,640 --> 00:18:23,750
You're saying I'm facing Starfleet Academy's

397
00:18:23,750 --> 00:18:27,560
unwinnable command scenario: the Kobayashi Maru.

398
00:18:27,560 --> 00:18:28,410
Exactly.

399
00:18:28,410 --> 00:18:29,780
Sometimes you can't win.

400
00:18:29,780 --> 00:18:31,940
Captain Kirk won.

401
00:18:33,150 --> 00:18:35,190
Kirk cheated.

402
00:18:36,550 --> 00:18:39,840
Impressive that you know that.

403
00:18:39,840 --> 00:18:43,280
It's hard to believe i'm actually having this conversation with you.

404
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:45,210
Right there with you.

405
00:18:46,260 --> 00:18:52,070
Kirk beat the Kobayashi Maru by reprogramming the simulator.

406
00:18:52,070 --> 00:18:53,850
- That's it. - What?

407
00:18:53,850 --> 00:18:56,610
- I'll reprogram Howard. - What...?

408
00:18:56,610 --> 00:18:58,860
Sheldon, you can't reprogram people.

409
00:18:58,860 --> 00:19:02,440
No, you can't reprogram people.

410
00:19:02,740 --> 00:19:05,560
To James Tiberius Kirk.

411
00:19:15,750 --> 00:19:17,340
Hello, all.

412
00:19:17,910 --> 00:19:22,310
Howard, you're feeling better about me today, aren't you?

413
00:19:22,310 --> 00:19:24,040
Not really.

414
00:19:24,040 --> 00:19:25,810
Yes, you are.

415
00:19:25,810 --> 00:19:27,880
I'm using neurolinguistic programming

416
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:30,350
to modify your thought patterns.

417
00:19:32,100 --> 00:19:34,180
Go away, Sheldon.

418
00:19:34,700 --> 00:19:37,870
There's a $9.95 e-book down the drain.

419
00:19:37,870 --> 00:19:38,950
What's in the bag?

420
00:19:38,950 --> 00:19:40,380
It's for Howard.

421
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:42,830
Oh. Sheldon, you can't fix this with gifts.

422
00:19:42,830 --> 00:19:44,400
Nevertheless, I've hurt you,

423
00:19:44,400 --> 00:19:48,130
and whether you forgive me or not, I want you to have this.

424
00:19:50,600 --> 00:19:52,850
You're giving me a couch cushion?

425
00:19:52,850 --> 00:19:53,360
No.

426
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:55,130
The cushion is merely symbolic.

427
00:19:55,130 --> 00:19:58,510
I'm giving you my spot on the couch.

428
00:20:00,270 --> 00:20:02,060
But you love that spot.

429
00:20:02,060 --> 00:20:04,680
No. I love my mother.

430
00:20:04,680 --> 00:20:08,080
My feelings for my spot are much greater.

431
00:20:09,260 --> 00:20:11,510
It is the singular location in space

432
00:20:11,510 --> 00:20:15,430
around which revolves my entire universe.

433
00:20:15,430 --> 00:20:17,760
And now it's yours.

434
00:20:18,180 --> 00:20:21,610
Oh, my God, dude. Now you have to forgive him.

435
00:20:23,060 --> 00:20:24,090
All right.

436
00:20:24,090 --> 00:20:26,720
Apology accepted.

437
00:20:26,720 --> 00:20:28,160
High five.

438
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:30,150
Not too hard.

439
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:33,210
Thank you.

440
00:20:33,210 --> 00:20:35,930
I haven't cried like this since Toy Story 3.

441
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:46,340
I got to tell you, Sheldon,

442
00:20:46,340 --> 00:20:48,540
I understand why you chose this spot.

443
00:20:48,540 --> 00:20:51,600
I mean, the temperature is good, but there's no draft.

444
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:53,890
I can see the television, but I can still talk to...

445
00:20:53,890 --> 00:20:56,020
I changed my mind. Get out of my spot.

446
00:20:58,120 --> 00:20:59,150
How long?

447
00:20:59,150 --> 00:21:01,060
94 seconds.

